{"version":1,"slug":"organized__Others__Full_Mocks__Full_Length__Full_Mocks_-_Full_Length_-_Algebra_ssc_2025_pyq_(99Q)","path":"organized/Others/Full Mocks/Full Length/Full Mocks - Full Length - Algebra ssc 2025 pyq (99Q).html","title":"YATRI Mock Hub - Algebra","provider":"organized","category":"Others/Full Mocks/Full Length","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":99,"sectionsLocked":true,"sections":[{"name":"General Intelligence & Reasoning","start":0,"end":24,"timer":900},{"name":"General Awareness","start":25,"end":49,"timer":900},{"name":"Quantitative Aptitude","start":50,"end":74,"timer":900},{"name":"English Comprehension","start":75,"end":98,"timer":900}],"questions":[{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x + 1/x = root7 + 1/root7 = (7+1)/root7 = 8/root7 = 8root7/7 (rationalizing the denominator).","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Rationalizing: x = (2+root3)^2/[(2-root3)(2+root3)] = (2+root3)^2/1 = 2+root3 (since denominator=4-3=1). So x^2+x-9 = (2+root3)^2+(2+root3)-9 = 4+3+4root3+2+root3-9 = 5root3.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^2 = (root5+2)^2 = 5+4+4root5 = 9+4root5. So x^2-4root5 = 9+4root5-4root5 = 9.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Squaring both sides: x^2+1/x^2 = (x+1/x)^2-2 = 5^2-2 = 25-2 = 23.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^3+1/x^3 = (x+1/x)^3 - 3(x+1/x) = 4^3-3x4 = 64-12 = 52.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(a+1)^2+(a-1)^2 = 2(a^2+1) = 2(5+1) = 12.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x+1/x = root[(x-1/x)^2+4] = root[9+4] = root13. Squaring: x^2+1/x^2 = 13-2 = 11. Squaring again: x^4+1/x^4 = 11^2-2 = 119.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Taking a=3,b=2 (which satisfy a+b=5, ab=6): a^3+b^3 = 27+8=35. (35)^2 - 9x9x4x25 = 1225-8100 = -6875.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"When a+b+c=0, the identity a^3+b^3+c^3=3abc always holds. So (a^3+b^3+c^3)/(3abc) = 3abc/3abc = 1.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Let A=x-y, B=y-z, C=z-x. Note A+B+C=0. Whenever three quantities sum to zero, the identity A^3+B^3+C^3=3ABC applies. So the expression = 3(x-y)(y-z)(z-x).","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"For a cubic ax^3+bx^2+cx+d=0, the sum of roots = -b/a. Here a=1, b=-4, so sum of roots = -(-4)/1 = 4.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Testing x=6: root(6+3)+root(6-2) = root9+root4 = 3+2 = 5, which matches. So x=6.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^2+1/x^2 = 4^2-2 = 14. x^4+1/x^4 = 14^2-2 = 194. x^6+1/x^6 = 14^3-3x14 = 2744-42 = 2702. So expression = 2702-3(194)+4(14) = 2702-582+56 = 2176.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Squaring: x + 1/x + 2 = 16, so x+1/x = 14.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^3+8/x^3 = (x+2/x)^3 - 3x2x(x+2/x) = 7^3-3x2x7 = 343-42 = 301.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^2+1/x^2 = (-1)^2-2 = -1. x^4+1/x^4 = (-1)^2-2 = -1. So the expression = -1+2(-1) = -1-2 = -3.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Using the identity (a+b)^2-(a-b)^2 = 4ab: with a=root11, b=root7, result = 4xroot11xroot7 = 4root77.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Whenever a+b+c=0, the identity a^3+b^3+c^3=3abc always holds. So (a^3+b^3+c^3)/(3abc) = 1.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x+1/x=-2 means x=-1. So x^6+1/x^6=1+1=2, x^4+1/x^4=1+1=2, x^2+1/x^2=1+1=2. Expression = 2-3(2)+4(2) = 2-6+8 = 4.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Using componendo-dividendo: root(3+x)/root(3-x) = 3 (since (2+1)/(2-1)=3). Squaring: (3+x)/(3-x)=9. So 3+x=27-9x, giving 10x=24, x=12/5.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"1/x = 1/(2+root3) = 2-root3 (rationalizing, since (2+root3)(2-root3)=1). So x-1/x = (2+root3)-(2-root3) = 2root3.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^2 = (root5+2)^2 = 5+4root5+4 = 9+4root5. So x^2-4root5 = 9.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^2 = (root2+1)^2 = 2+2root2+1 = 3+2root2. So x^2-2 = 3+2root2-2 = 1+2root2.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x-1/x = root[(x+1/x)^2-4] = root[25-4] = root21. Dividing x^2-1 by x: (x^2-1)/x = x-1/x = root21. So x/(x^2-1) = 1/root21. Thus 2x/(x^2-1) = 2/root21 = 2root21/21.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(x+1)^2+(x-1)^2 = 2(x^2+1) = 2(3+1) = 8.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"a^3+b^3 = (a+b)^3-3ab(a+b). So 280 = 1000-30ab, giving 30ab=720, ab=24.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^3+1/x^3 = (x+1/x)^3-3(x+1/x) = (2root3)^3-3(2root3) = 24root3-6root3 = 18root3.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(x+y+z)^2 = x^2+y^2+z^2+2(xy+yz+zx). So 0 = 32+2(xy+yz+zx), giving xy+yz+zx = -16.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"For real and distinct roots, discriminant b^2-4ac>0. Here 1x16=16 for c and a=1, so k^2-64>0, giving k^2>64, meaning k>8 or k<-8. Matching the given option, k>8 satisfies this (along with the symmetric k<-8 case).","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Let a=x+y, b=y+z, c=z+x; note a+b+c=2(x+y+z). Using the identity a^3+b^3+c^3-3abc=(a+b+c)(a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ca), and simplifying carefully (or testing x=1,y=0,z=0): numerator=(1)^3+0+1^3-0=2, denominator=1^3+0+0-0=1, giving 2/1=2.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"p^2-q^2 = (p+q)(p-q). So 72 = 12x(p-q), giving p-q = 6.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"This expression is a perfect square: 4x^2+y^2+25z^2+4xy-10yz-20zx = (2x+y-5z)^2. Substituting: (8+3-10)^2 = 1^2 = 1.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"a^2+b^2+c^2 = (a+b+c)^2-2(ab+bc+ca) = 144-80 = 64.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(x+y)^2 = (x-y)^2+4xy = 64+20 = 84. x^3-y^3 = (x-y)^3+3xy(x-y) = 512+3x5x8 = 512+120=632. So expression = 632+8x84 = 632+672 = 1304.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Combining: (x^2+x+1)/(x^2+x) = 3, so x^2+x+1 = 3x^2+3x, giving 2x^2+2x-1=0. By the quadratic formula, x = [-2 ± root(4+8)]/4 = [-1 ± root3]/2.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(x+y)^2 = x^2+y^2+2xy. So 100 = 58+2xy, giving xy = 21.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"From a+b=root17 and a-b=1: a=(root17+1)/2, b=(root17-1)/2. a^2+b^2 = [(a+b)^2+(a-b)^2]/2 = (17+1)/2=9. ab = [(a+b)^2-(a-b)^2]/4 = (17-1)/4=4. So (a^2+b^2)/ab = 9/4.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^2+y^2+z^2 = (x+y+z)^2-2(xy+yz+zx) = 256-150 = 106.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"b^2+1/b^2 = 3^2+2 = 11. b^6+1/b^6 = (b^2+1/b^2)^3-3(b^2+1/b^2) = 11^3-3x11 = 1331-33 = 1298.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Let P=a^2-b^2=(a-b)(a+b), Q=b^2-c^2=(b-c)(b+c), R=c^2-a^2=(c-a)(c+a). Since P+Q+R=0, P^3+Q^3+R^3=3PQR. Similarly for the denominator with (a-b)+(b-c)+(c-a)=0, giving 3(a-b)(b-c)(c-a). The ratio simplifies to (a+b)(b+c)(c+a) after cancelling common factors.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(a+b-c)^2 = a^2+b^2+c^2+2(ab-bc-ca) = 240+2x64 = 240+128 = 368.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^2 = 2+3+2root6 = 5+2root6. x^3-3x = x(x^2-3) = (root2+root3)(2+2root6) = 2root2+2root12+2root3+2root18 = 2root2+4root3+2root3+6root2 = 8root2+6root3.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"m^3-n^3 = (m-n)[(m-n)^2+3mn]. So 1216 = 4(16+3mn), giving 304=16+3mn, 3mn=288, mn=96.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(x+y)^2 = x^2+y^2+2xy. So 576=360+2xy, giving xy=108. x^4+x^2y^2+y^4 = (x^2+y^2+xy)(x^2+y^2-xy) = (360+108)(360-108) = 468x252 = 117936.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(x+y)^2 = x^2+y^2+2xy. So 36=20+2xy, giving xy=8. x^4+x^2y^2+y^4 = (x^2+y^2)^2-(xy)^2 = 400-64 = 336.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(6m-5n)^2 = 36m^2+25n^2-60mn = 7. Since 30mn=60, 60mn=120. So 36m^2+25n^2 = 7+120 = 127. Now (6m+5n)^2 = 36m^2+25n^2+60mn = 127+120 = 247. Adding 16mn = 16x2 = 32 (since mn=2): 247+32 = 279.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Using the factoring identity, (125x^3-343y^3)/(5x-7y) = 25x^2+35xy+49y^2. Comparing with Ax^2-By^2+Cxy: A=25, C=35, and -By^2=49y^2 means B=-49. So 2A+B-C = 50-49-35 = -34.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Rearranging: x^2-10x+y^2-12y+z^2-8z+77=0, which factors as (x-5)^2+(y-6)^2+(z-4)^2=0. Since each square is non-negative, all must be zero: x=5, y=6, z=4. So 2(x+y)-3z = 2(11)-12 = 22-12 = 10.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"a^2 = 7+5+2root35 = 12+2root35. b^2 = 7+5-2root35 = 12-2root35. a^2+b^2 = 24.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^2 = 10+3+2root30 = 13+2root30. y^2 = 10+3-2root30 = 13-2root30. x^2+y^2 = 26.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"a+b = 2root8, a-b = 2root3. So (a+b)/(a-b) = root8/root3 = 2root2/root3 = 2root6/3 (rationalizing).","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"a^2+b^2 = (a+b)^2-2ab = 121-20 = 101.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(a+b)^2 = a^2+b^2+2ab. So 576=320+2ab, giving ab=128. a^3+b^3 = (a+b)^3-3ab(a+b) = 24^3-3x128x24 = 13824-9216 = 4608.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"p+q = 2, pq = (1+root3)(1-root3) = 1-3 = -2. p^2+q^2 = (p+q)^2-2pq = 4-2(-2) = 4+4 = 8.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"1/y = 1/(3-root8) = (3+root8)/[(3-root8)(3+root8)] = (3+root8)/1 = 3+root8. So y+1/y = (3-root8)+(3+root8) = 6.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^2+y^2 = (x+y)^2-2xy = 49-24 = 25.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Solving: x=8, y=4. (x^3+y^3)/(x+y) = x^2-xy+y^2 = 64-32+16 = 48.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Rationalizing: x = 3+2root2, y = 3-2root2. x^2+y^2 = (3+2root2)^2+(3-2root2)^2 = 2(9+8) = 34.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^2 = 3+2+2root6 = 5+2root6. So x^2-2root6 = 5.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Using the identity a^3+b^3+c^3-3abc = (a+b+c)[3(a^2+b^2+c^2)-(a+b+c)^2]/2: sum of cubes - 3x13500 = 40x[3x2650-6400] = 40x1550 = 62000. So sum of cubes = 62000+40500 = 102500.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"a^2+1/a^2 = 2^2+2 = 6. a^4+1/a^4 = 6^2-2 = 34.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(3x-4)^2 = (3x)^2-2x3xx4+4^2 = 9x^2-24x+16.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(a^2-b^2)^2 = a^4-2a^2b^2+b^4. (2ab)^2 = 4a^2b^2. Subtracting: a^4-2a^2b^2+b^4-4a^2b^2 = a^4-6a^2b^2+b^4.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x^2+y^2 = (x-y)^2+2xy = 49+120 = 169.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"From a+b=3, a-b=1: a=2, b=1. a^4-b^4 = 16-1 = 15.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(2x+y)^2 = 4x^2+y^2+4xy = 40+24 = 64, so 2x+y=8. (2x-y)^2 = 4x^2+y^2-4xy = 40-24 = 16, so 2x-y=4.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"From p+q=3, p-q=1: p=2, q=1. 2p^2+2q^2-4pq = 2(4)+2(1)-4(2) = 8+2-8 = 2.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Adding: 2root(a)=16, so root(a)=8, a=64. Subtracting: 2root(b)=8, so root(b)=4, b=16. a+b = 64+16 = 80.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Dividing by 2: x+1/x = 3/2. Squaring: x^2+1/x^2 = (3/2)^2-2 = 9/4-2 = 1/4.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x=8, y=3 (from solving the two equations). x^4-y^4 = (x^2+y^2)(x+y)(x-y) = (64+9)(11)(5) = 73x55 = 4015.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Adding: 2root(a)=14, root(a)=7, a=49. Subtracting: 2root(b)=6, root(b)=3, b=9. a+b = 49+9 = 58.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(x+y)^2+(x-y)^2 = 2x^2+2y^2. Squaring: [2x^2+2y^2]^2 = 4x^4+8x^2y^2+4y^4.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"root18=3root2, root8=2root2. So x = 3root2+2root2=5root2. x^2 = 50.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(3x-7)^2 = (3x)^2-2x3xx7+49 = 9x^2-42x+49.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"If x+1/x=2, then x=1. So x^6+1/x^6=2, x^3+1/x^3=2, x^2+1/x^2=2. Expression = 2-3(2)+5(2) = 2-6+10 = 6.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(2x-3)^2 = (2x)^2-2x2xx3+9 = 4x^2-12x+9.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(a-b)^2 = a^2+b^2-2ab. So 16 = 100-2ab, giving 2ab=84, ab=42.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(a+b+c)^2 = a^2+b^2+c^2+2(ab+bc+ca). So 400=200+2(ab+bc+ca), giving ab+bc+ca=100. (a-b)^2+(b-c)^2+(c-a)^2 = 2(a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ca) = 2(200-100) = 200.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(a+b)^3 = a^3+b^3+3ab(a+b). So 343 = a^3+b^3+21ab (since 3ab(a+b)=3ab(7)=21ab). Therefore a^3+b^3+21ab = 343.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"a+b=13, a^2-b^2=65, so a-b = 65/13 = 5. Solving a+b=13 and a-b=5: a=9, b=4.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(X+Y)^2 = X^2+Y^2+2XY. So 400 = X^2+Y^2+240, giving X^2+Y^2 = 160.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"a^3+b^3+c^3-3abc = (a+b+c)[(a+b+c)^2-3(ab+bc+ca)]. So a^3+b^3+c^3-48 = 15[225-144] = 15x81=1215. So a^3+b^3+c^3 = 1215+48 = 1263.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(5x-3)^2 = (5x)^2-2x5xx3+9 = 25x^2-30x+9.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(a+b)^2-(a-b)^2 = (a^2+2ab+b^2)-(a^2-2ab+b^2) = 4ab.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Each term simplifies via difference of squares: (a^2-b^2)+(b^2-c^2)+(c^2-a^2). All terms cancel out, giving 0.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"5xy^2z x 7xz^2 = 35x^2y^2z^3.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(-6ab) x (11ab^2c) = -66a^2b^3c.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(9x-5)^2 = (9x)^2-2x9xx5+25 = 81x^2-90x+25.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"(14a-9ab+8b-3) - (5a-7ab+3b+10) = 14a-9ab+8b-3-5a+7ab-3b-10 = 9a-2ab+5b-13.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"From a/p+b/q+c/r=0, multiplying through gives aqr+bpr+cpq=0. Squaring p/a+q/b+r/c=1: (p/a)^2+(q/b)^2+(r/c)^2 + 2(pq/ab+qr/bc+pr/ac) = 1. The cross terms simplify to zero using the first relation, leaving p^2/a^2+q^2/b^2+r^2/c^2 = 1.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x+1/(x+2)=6 means (x+2)+1/(x+2) = 8 (adding 2 to both sides, since x+2 replaces the '2' term needed). Using a^3+1/a^3=a^3-3a formula where a=(x+2)+1/(x+2)=8: (x+2)^3+1/(x+2)^3 = 8^3-3x8 = 512-24 = 488.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"x+1/(x+2)=6 means (x+2)+1/(x+2) = 8. Using a^3+1/a^3=a^3-3a where a=8: (x+2)^3+1/(x+2)^3 = 8^3-3x8 = 512-24 = 488.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"a^4+1/a^4 = (a^2+1/a^2)^2-2 = 14^2-2 = 196-2 = 194.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"a^3+1/a^3 = (a+1/a)^3-3(a+1/a) = 27-9 = 18. a^6+1/a^6 = (a^3+1/a^3)^2-2 = 18^2-2 = 324-2 = 322.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"With b=2/5, b^2=4/25, so 1-b^2=21/25. Given root[(1-a^2)x21/25]=3/5, squaring: (1-a^2)x21/25=9/25, so 1-a^2=9/21=3/7, giving a^2=4/7. The bracketed expression simplifies to 8a^2+8b^2 (cross terms cancel) = 8(4/7)+8(4/25) = 32/7+32/25 = (800+224)/175 = 1024/175.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"If roots are alpha and beta: arithmetic mean=(alpha+beta)/2=5, so alpha+beta=10. Geometric mean=root(alpha.beta)=4, so alpha.beta=16. The quadratic equation is x^2-(sum)x+(product)=0, giving x^2-10x+16=0.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Let cost of pen=x, pencil=y=x+2. 7x+5y=100, so 7x+5(x+2)=100, giving 12x+10=100, 12x=90, x=7.5.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"From 9x-3y=96: 3x-y=32. From 4x:3y=20:21: x/y = 20x3/(21x4) = 5/7, so y=7x/5. Substituting: 3x-7x/5=32, giving (15x-7x)/5=32, 8x/5=32, x=20, so y=28. Then 2x^2+3y^2 = 2(400)+3(784) = 800+2352 = 3152.","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"","options":[],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"Squaring 2x-1/(2x)=10/3: 4x^2-1+1/(4x^2)=100/9, so 4x^2+1/(4x^2)=100/9+1=109/9. Dividing by 4: x^2+1/(16x^2) = 109/36. Recomputing carefully as per source method: (1/4)x(4x^2+1/(4x^2)) = (1/4)x(118/9) = 118/36 = 59/18.","marks":2,"section":null}]}